<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06RX">Example <span data-tag="06RX">4.7.9.24</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $X$ be an object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. If $X$ is discrete, then the canonical map $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/X} )} \rightarrow (\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}})_{/X}$ is an equivalence of categories. This follows by applying Corollary <a data-tag="05K4" href="/tag/05K4">4.7.9.23</a> in the special case $n = 1$ (see Example <a data-tag="0599" href="/tag/0599">4.7.9.3</a>). </p>
</article>
